q q 0 .027451 .466667 rg BT 8.4 TL/F1 7 Tf 1 0 0 1 45.35433 22.67717 Tm T* ET BT 1 0 0 1 527.7383 22.67717 Tm T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 771.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 22 TL/F2 18 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm (4. Evidence-Based Business Recommendations)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 745.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 16 TL/F2 12.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3.5 Tm (Treat airport markets as a distinct commercial segment.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 712.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 13.5 TL/F1 9.3 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 17.7 Tm (Monitor JFK and LaGuardia separately because their recorded revenue per trip is substantially higher than ordinary)Tj T* (Manhattan markets.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 689.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 16 TL/F2 12.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3.5 Tm (Manage Manhattan using both volume and value.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 656.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 13.5 TL/F1 9.3 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 17.7 Tm (Use both trips and revenue/trip so high-volume, lower-value zones are not treated the same as high-volume,)Tj T* (higher-value zones.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 633.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 16 TL/F2 12.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3.5 Tm (Use revenue per trip-hour as an operational KPI.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 613.8701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 13.5 TL/F1 9.3 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4.2 Tm (Assess trip value alongside time utilisation rather than relying only on average revenue per trip.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 590.8701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 16 TL/F2 12.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3.5 Tm (Plan capacity around peak periods.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 557.8701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 13.5 TL/F1 9.3 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 17.7 Tm (The strongest demand occurs in the afternoon/evening, with 18:00 the peak trip-volume hour and 17:00 the peak)Tj T* (total-revenue hour.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 534.8701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 16 TL/F2 12.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3.5 Tm (Monitor the 2026 shift.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 515.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 13.5 TL/F1 9.3 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4.2 Tm <547261636b2074686520686967686572204a616e964a756c203230323620726576656e75652f74726970206279206d6f6e74682c207a6f6e6520616e64207472697020747970652074